@startuml
actor "ESP32 or IoT simulator" as Device
actor Operator
participant "Telemetry REST API" as API
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Operations Portal" as Portal

Device -> API : POST /api/v1/telemetry/temperature
note right of Device
JSON: machineId, temperature, humidity,
doorOpen, sensorOk
Auth: X-Device-Key or staff JWT
end note
API -> API : authenticate key / staff role
API -> DB : insert TemperatureLog and update Machine / lastPing
DB --> API : persisted measurement and state
API --> Portal : SSE telemetry event
Portal -> API : reload alerts / fleet / history
API --> Portal : updated operations data

Operator -> API : POST /machines/{id}/clear-fault
API -> DB : verify FAULT and latest safe telemetry <= 2 min
alt safe telemetry, door closed and temperature in range
  API -> DB : set ONLINE and write MachineAction audit
  API --> Operator : fault cleared
else unsafe, stale or missing telemetry
  API --> Operator : 409; keep machine in FAULT
end

note over Device,Portal
Device uplink is HTTP REST, not MQTT or WebSocket.
Dashboard updates use SSE plus 30-second polling fallback.
end note
@enduml
